Package: defxbridge
Type: Package
Title: Extract DEFX Documentation Tags from SAS and R Programs
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Param", "Madan", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "86084060+parammadan@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: An independent R prototype inspired by the published DEFX tag
    concept (Bartley and Hinger, PharmaSUG 2026, AP-220). Reads structured
    DEFX documentation comments from SAS and R source files, normalizes them
    into one provenance-preserving metadata table, validates them against an
    explicit specification, and fills a synthetic define-like Excel workbook.
    Not affiliated with or endorsed by CBAR or PharmaSUG; not a validated or
    regulatory-certified tool.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports: openxlsx, stats, tools, utils
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), readxl, withr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
